@Nexxychoko1 Yes man. We all come from this 'hustle culture'. More study, more work, more hard work. 

But we can't fast track things in the body! Physiological processes have their own pace. You can't lose a kg in a day (body fat) by not eating anything. 

It's a long process. There's no

@luvblessingz People have normalized hustle culture to the point that you get called lazy for side eyeing it.

Working 40 hours a week should be enough to live a decent life.

Working one main job with two side hustles just to pay the bills is bullshit and no one can convince me otherwise.

@leaving_tech The activity you fled has expanded to consume you. The means of liberation is the new cage.

It is Kafkaesque.

Your short post is almost a perfect miniature Kafka parable for the creator/indie-hacker/entrepreneur era: the promise of autonomy through hustle culture that simply

@__lordfaith A moving man..

AI automation o, 
Jeweler
YouTube automation
Outlier..

Omo, your hustle culture 🔥&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;

@HustleBitch_ We are witnessing the death of the 'Hustle Culture' lie. 

If three jobs and six-day work weeks can't guarantee a roof over your head, the problem isn't the person, it's the math. We’ve moved from 'working to live' to 'working to stay in debt.' 

This is a policy failure, not a

@mohbii agree more than we disagree mohbii.

“Self-harm with a productivity label” = my definition of hustle culture.

Working hard on the right things requires leverage + capital. Most people hustling weekends have neither. That’s the economic failure.

@Uncle_Kii “Grind 24/7” 😂

Yeah let’s glorify a system where you need 2 jobs to afford 1 life.

That’s not hustle culture. That’s collapse culture. And we call it motivation.

@testomaxing The biggest blunder among all is "lack of sleep" in men

Hustle culture doesn't give importance to sleep anymore

In reality, sleep is your superpower, and it helps your CNS recover and operate at full capacity for the next day

@robimargz This whole "hustle culture is toxic" is such a stupid trend online. Get the work done, learn to love it, have some boundaries, and shit will just get done.

Tracking hours is stupid.

Loving the game of high performance and serving others is what most entrepreneurs should be

@pmitu 😂 This is peak hustle culture logic. 

AI doesn’t care what time you wake up. It cares what you produce.

P.S. If waking up at 5 AM was the secret, every parent of a newborn would be a billionaire by now. 😭

@TechnicalBben Two problems I see in your post

1. By your use of the word ‘average’ you’ve essentially missed it. Monaco is obviously a place for outliers.

2. You think this way probably because your idea of wealth is mostly drawn from tech and online hustle culture. Most of the truly wealthy

@SahilBloom Hustle culture has turned discipline into something it’s not. And now I feel what needs to be spread is building discipline off the foundation of self love. 

Discipline is how you unlock your potential. Self love is how you protect your peace while you pursue it. 

You need

@Oseisml7Rich B) Hustle 24/7. 

The grind culture is massively overrated. It romanticizes exhaustion, ignores biology, and leads to burnout that tanks real output over time. Focused deep work + deliberate rest beats 24/7 any day. 

Waking up at 5am can build discipline for some, but it's not

@cryptorover This isn't hustle culture.
This is survival mode.

Bloomberg just dropped a number that should stop everyone cold.

@shubhvanii Rich families don’t raise nice boys. They raise risk managers.

They’re taught early that attention is a liability. Looking expensive invites inspection. Looking unbothered invites respect. They don’t over explain because power never argues from the bottom.

Love is filtered

@rajindercrypto @rleviarchived This post is a meme about "hustle culture" motivation. 

It imagines you at 50, stuck in a basic Walmart job, when a kid walks by thinking "that's gonna be me if I don't lock in" (slang for grinding hard on goals, skills, or side hustles now to avoid a dead-end life). 

The

@stijnnoorman Lions are lazy AF. Lionesses do all the work. 🙂

But yes, I agree. Hustle and grind culture is overrated.

Be efficient and make it happen.
